---
/** Lunescence's window. Placeholder voice and branding until its own window is authored. */
---

<section class="frame sec lift" data-placeholder="project-window" aria-labelledby="lune-h">
  <div class="lune" data-reveal="scene">
    <div>
      <h2 class="kicker" id="lune-h" style="color:#9cc9d9;margin:0;font-weight:400">Lunescence</h2>
      <p class="ui" style="margin:8px 0 0;font-style:italic;font-size:14px;color:#9cc9d9">An imagined moment.</p>
      <p style="margin:26px 0 0;font-size:clamp(22px,2.3vw,32px);line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:-.01em;max-width:30ch;font-variation-settings:'opsz' 36">
        <span class="scene-line" style="transition-delay:.3s">You say something unexpected.</span>
        <span class="scene-line" style="transition-delay:1.5s">Before the reply, there’s a glance, a change of expression,</span>
        <span class="scene-line" style="transition-delay:2.7s">a small gesture you start to recognise.</span>
      </p>
      <p style="margin:28px 0 0;font-size:17px;color:#c9d4dc;max-width:48ch">Lunescence is my idea for a 3D AI companion: expressive, recognisable, and full of small particularities. I want to explore what happens when its words, movements and personality belong to the same character.</p>
      <p class="ui" style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:14px;color:#8fa3b0">Early concept. Currently paused.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="moon" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</section>
